# /new-rn-component -- Generate a React Native Component

## What This Does

Generates a new React Native component following project conventions: TypeScript
interface for props, {{ ui }} for styles (`.claude/styles/{% if ui == 'StyleSheet' %}stylesheet{% elif ui == 'NativeWind' %}nativewind{% elif ui == 'Tamagui' %}tamagui{% else %}gluestack{% endif %}.md`), theme
{{ 'constants' if ui == 'StyleSheet' else 'tokens' }} for colours and spacing, and platform-specific considerations.

## Usage

```
/new-rn-component TransactionCard              # List item component
/new-rn-component BudgetProgressBar            # UI primitive
/new-rn-component FilterChip --dir=ui          # In src/components/ui/
/new-rn-component CategoryBadge --dir=lists    # In src/components/lists/
/new-rn-component LoginForm --dir=forms        # In src/components/forms/
```

## Arguments

| Argument | Required | Description |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| `name`   | Yes      | Component name in PascalCase (e.g., `TransactionCard`) |
| `--dir`  | No       | Subdirectory under `src/components/`. Default: `ui` |

## How It Works

### 1. Determine File Location

Place the component file at:
```
src/components/<dir>/<ComponentName>.tsx
```

Default directory is `ui`. Common directories:
- `ui/` -- Reusable UI primitives (Button, Card, TextInput, Badge)
- `lists/` -- List item components (TransactionCard, BudgetRow)
- `forms/` -- Form-specific components (CurrencyInput, DatePicker)
- `layout/` -- Layout wrappers (Section, Divider, SafeContainer)

### 2. Generate the Component

Create the component with:
- TypeScript `interface` for props (exported)
- Functional component with destructured props
{% if ui == 'StyleSheet' %}
- `StyleSheet.create()` at the bottom of the file + theme constants from `@/constants`
{% elif ui == 'NativeWind' %}
- `className` utility classes from the Tailwind theme; variants switch whole class strings
{% elif ui == 'Tamagui' %}
- Tamagui primitives (`XStack`, `YStack`, `SizableText`) and `styled()` variants with `$tokens`
{% else %}
- The generated gluestack-ui components from `@/components/ui/*` (add missing ones with
  `npx gluestack-ui@latest add <name>`), `className` with semantic colour classes, `tva` variants
{% endif %}
- Platform-specific handling where relevant
- Optional `testID` prop for testing; accessibility label / role on interactive elements
- No `React.memo` / `useCallback` wrapping: the React Compiler memoizes (add one only for a
  measured problem, with a comment); `ref` as a normal prop, no `forwardRef`

See `references/rn-component-examples.md` for {{ ui }} templates.

### 3. Generate Test File

Create a corresponding test file at:
```
__tests__/components/<dir>/<ComponentName>.test.tsx
```

With basic tests for:
- Default rendering
- Props handling
- User interactions (if interactive)

### 4. Verify

```bash
npx tsc --noEmit
```

## Component Conventions

### Props Interface

```typescript
// Always export the props interface
export interface TransactionCardProps {
  transaction: Transaction;
  onPress?: (id: string) => void;
  testID?: string;
}
```

{% if ui == 'StyleSheet' %}
### Styles

```typescript
// Always at the bottom of the file
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    // Use theme constants, never hardcoded values
    padding: spacing.md,
    backgroundColor: colors.surface,
    borderRadius: borderRadius.md,
  },
});
```

### Theme Constants

Always import from `@/constants`:
```typescript
import { colors, spacing, typography, borderRadius, shadows } from '@/constants';
```
{% elif ui == 'NativeWind' %}
### Styles

- Theme colours and spacing from `tailwind.config.js`; no arbitrary `[#hex]` values
- Conditional styles pick between whole class strings:
  `className={isExpense ? 'text-red-600' : 'text-green-600'}`
- Accept a `className` prop on layout components so callers can add margins
{% elif ui == 'Tamagui' %}
### Styles

- Reusable look = `styled(YStack | XStack | Text, { ..., variants })`, typed with `GetProps`
- Values are tokens (`$md`, `$4`, `$background`, `$color10`); press/hover via `pressStyle` / `hoverStyle`
- No `StyleSheet.create` next to Tamagui components
{% else %}
### Styles

- Edit or compose the generated components; new variants go in a `tva` definition
- Semantic colour classes (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`); no hex values
- State styles through `data-[active=true]:` / `data-[disabled=true]:` classes
{% endif %}

### List Items

Components rendered in FlashList `renderItem` are plain function components; keep
them light (no per-row data crunching) and let the React Compiler memoize them.
